# (git ignores .env – never commit a real token).
#
# Until Registration's login is ready (SH-S01), the console uses one fixed JWT.
# Make one from the repo root (it is signed with the same key the API checks):
#
#   dotnet user-jwts create --project backend --role "emergency:Admin" --name "Demo Admin"
#
# Use emergency:Admin for the full demo (closing calls needs Admin or Responder, test weather needs Admin).
# emergency:Dispatcher or emergency:Viewer show what those roles can see.
# The token is built into the app, so after changing it rebuild: docker compose up --build frontend
VITE_API_TOKEN= 